# Clojure Style & Review Rules

Enforced during code review (Bhishma) and code authoring (Parth). Based on the Helpshift Clojure Style Guide — a fork of https://guide.clojure.style/ with Helpshift-specific conventions.

> **Companion reference:** `~/.cursor/rules/clojure-daily-tips.mdc` is a lightweight quick-reference covering the most common layout / `ns` / indentation rules for daily programming. Use it for fast lookups. This file (`clojure-review.mdc`) is the **authoritative** reference — if the two ever disagree, this one wins.

Severity mapping:
- 🔴 **CRITICAL** — bug risk, correctness issue, or unsafe side effect (block merge)
- 🟠 **HIGH** — idiomatic/clarity violation that will confuse readers or hide bugs
- 🟡 **MEDIUM** — readability / maintainability
- 🔵 **LOW** — style / nitpick

---

## 1. Source Code Layout

### 1.1 Max line length — 🔵 LOW
- Keep lines ≤ 80 chars where feasible. Team-wide consensus may raise to 100 or 120. Never go beyond 120.

### 1.2 Spaces, not tabs — 🟡 MEDIUM
- Indent with spaces. No hard tabs.

### 1.3 Body indentation — 🟡 MEDIUM
- Use **2 spaces** to indent the bodies of `def*`, special forms, and body-form macros (`let`, `loop`, `when`, `when-let`, `cond`, `as->`, `cond->`, `case`, `with-*`, etc.).

### 1.4 Function argument alignment — 🟡 MEDIUM
- When arguments span multiple lines **and the first arg is on the same line as the fn name**, vertically align args with the first arg:
```clojure
(filter even?
        (range 1 10))   ; ✅
```
- When no args are on the same line as the fn name, use **single-space indent** from the opening paren:
```clojure
(filter
 even?
 (range 1 10))          ; ✅
```

### 1.5 `let`/binding vector alignment — 🟡 MEDIUM
```clojure
(let [thing1 "some stuff"
      thing2 "other stuff"]
  ...)                  ; ✅
```

### 1.6 Map key alignment — 🟡 MEDIUM
```clojure
{:thing1 thing1
 :thing2 thing2}        ; ✅
```

### 1.7 Bracket spacing — 🟡 MEDIUM
- One space separates text from brackets externally; no internal padding.
```clojure
(foo (bar baz) quux)    ; ✅
(foo(bar baz)quux)      ; ❌
(foo ( bar baz ) quux)  ; ❌
```

### 1.8 No commas in sequential literals — 🔵 LOW
```clojure
[1 2 3]                 ; ✅
[1, 2, 3]               ; ❌
```
- Optional commas in map literals are fine if they aid readability.

### 1.9 Gather trailing parens — 🟡 MEDIUM
- Trailing parens collapse onto the same line. Exception: `(comment ...)` rich-comment blocks may keep the closing paren on its own line.

### 1.10 Empty lines between top-level forms — 🔵 LOW
- Use **two blank lines** between top-level forms. Grouping of related `def`s is an allowed exception.

### 1.11 No blank lines inside definitions — 🟡 MEDIUM
- No blank lines inside a `defn`/`defmacro` body. If you need separation, the function is probably too big — refactor. Exception: `cond`/`let` pair separation when they span multiple lines.

### 1.12 Trailing whitespace — 🔵 LOW
- Strip all trailing whitespace.

### 1.13 Unix line endings + terminal newline — 🔵 LOW
- LF line endings. Every file ends with a newline.

