## 3. Naming

### 3.1 Use `kebab-case` for everything — 🟡 MEDIUM
- Functions, vars, keywords, namespace segments.
```clojure
(def user-name "Alice")                        ; ✅
(def user_name "Alice")                        ; ❌
(def apiResponse {:eventType "a"})             ; ❌
```

### 3.2 Predicate functions end with `?` — 🟠 HIGH
```clojure
(valid-user? user)        ; ✅
(archived? report)        ; ✅
(is-valid-user user)      ; ❌
(has-permission user)     ; ❌
```

### 3.3 Side-effecting / STM-unsafe functions end with `!` — 🟠 HIGH
- Mutations, I/O, `reset!`, `swap!`, `alter`, `send`, sending emails, writing files, DB writes.
```clojure
(save-user! user)         ; ✅
(send-email! to subj body); ✅
```

### 3.4 No `get-` / `is-` / `has-` / `can-` prefixes — 🟡 MEDIUM
```clojure
(defn user-name [user] ...)   ; ✅
(defn get-user-name [...])    ; ❌
```

### 3.5 Conversion fns use `->`, not `-to-` — 🔵 LOW
```clojure
(defn f->c [f] ...)           ; ✅
(defn f-to-c [f] ...)         ; ❌
```

### 3.6 `CapitalCase` for protocols, records, structs, types — 🟠 HIGH
- Acronyms stay uppercase: `HTTPClient`, `XMLParser`.

### 3.7 Earmuffs for dynamic vars — 🟠 HIGH
```clojure
(def ^:dynamic *request* nil)   ; ✅
(def ^:dynamic request nil)     ; ❌
```

### 3.8 No special notation for constants — 🔵 LOW
```clojure
(def max-size 10)         ; ✅
(def MAX-SIZE 10)         ; ❌ Java-style
(def +max-size+ 10)       ; ❌ CL-style
```

### 3.9 Unused bindings use `_` — 🟡 MEDIUM
- Preferred: `_name` (named but prefixed) when the name aids readability.
```clojure
(defn handler [ctx _user] ...)         ; ✅
(defn handler [ctx {:keys [id] :as _user}] ...) ; ✅
(dotimes [_ 3] (println "hi"))         ; ✅
```

### 3.10 Idiomatic parameter names — 🔵 LOW
Follow `clojure.core`:
- `f g h` — fn input
- `n` — integer size
- `i index` — integer index
- `x y` — numbers
- `xs` — sequence
- `m` — map
- `k ks` — key(s)
- `v vs` — value(s)
- `s` — string
- `re` — regex
- `sym` — symbol
- `coll` — collection
- `pred` — predicate
- `& more` — variadic
- `xf` — transducer
- `ns` — namespace
- Macros: `expr`, `body`, `binding`
- Methods: `this` for first arg in `defprotocol`/`deftype`/`defrecord`/`reify`

