## 4. Functions

### 4.1 Length ≤ 10 LOC — 🟡 MEDIUM
- Ideal target: ≤ 5 LOC. Longer = refactor candidate.

### 4.2 Max 3–4 positional parameters — 🟡 MEDIUM
- More than 4 → pass a map.

### 4.3 Prefer pre/post conditions over in-body checks — 🟡 MEDIUM
```clojure
(defn foo [x]
  {:pre [(pos? x)]}
  (bar x))                 ; ✅
```

### 4.4 Multi-arity order: fewest args → most — 🟡 MEDIUM
```clojure
(defn foo
  ([x]   (foo x 1))
  ([x y] (+ x y)))         ; ✅
```

### 4.5 Optional newline after fn name — 🔵 LOW
- Either of these is fine:
```clojure
(defn foo [x] (bar x))

(defn foo
  [x]
  (bar x))
```
- Bad: arg vector on same line when body is separate:
```clojure
(defn foo
  [x] (bar x))             ; ❌
```

### 4.6 Multimethod `dispatch-val` placement — 🔵 LOW
```clojure
(defmethod foo :bar [x] (baz x))   ; ✅ single line
(defmethod foo :bar                ; ✅ multi-line
  [x]
  (baz x))
```

### 4.7 Multi-arity body indentation — 🔵 LOW
- Each arity body indents aligned with its params (2 extra spaces past the arity's opening paren).

### 4.8 Docstring placement — 🟠 HIGH
- Docstring goes **after the fn name**, before the arg vector. Placing it inside the body does NOT attach it to the var.
```clojure
(defn foo "docstring" [x] (bar x))    ; ✅
(defn foo [x] "docstring" (bar x))    ; ❌
```

### 4.9 Mark private vars/fns — 🟡 MEDIUM
```clojure
(defn- helper [] ...)           ; ✅
(def ^:private thing ...)       ; ✅
(defn ^:private helper [] ...)  ; ❌ verbose
```
- To access a private var from outside (e.g., tests), use `@#'some.ns/var`.

